            {
                "entry_id": "0ca4b1fc-7f78-3037-8ae3-7981507d040d",
                "word": "taiga",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d71f4857-81e1-4c24-96e0-efaa62f128d6",
                        "entry_id": "0ca4b1fc-7f78-3037-8ae3-7981507d040d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "taigas"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
                        "entry_id": "0ca4b1fc-7f78-3037-8ae3-7981507d040d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A subarctic zone of evergreen coniferous forests situated south of the tundras and north of the steppes in the Northern Hemisphere."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d2cf569-b5db-41b0-b1f6-cdf6e96d6a31",
                                "sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
                                "text": "Like the taiga, he was everywhere, and mysterious—a heroic being with unearthly gifts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76e4c683-9e0e-4ed8-be67-d2e0916241ca",
                                "sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
                                "text": "The mountains run from the Arctic Island of Novaya Zemlya southwards, dividing the endless wastes of the Siberian taiga and the steppes from the Russian platform in the west."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35b849c9-50a8-4365-8f5c-78e5df195440",
                                "sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
                                "text": "Reindeer are well suited to the taiga’s frigid winters. They can maintain a thermogradient between body core and the environment of up to 100 degrees, in part because of insulation provided by their fur, and in part because of counter-current vascular heat exchange systems in their legs and nasal passages."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23aac162-672c-4fa4-ba06-36decbcf7058",
                        "source_entry_id": "0ca4b1fc-7f78-3037-8ae3-7981507d040d",
                        "source_sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
                        "source_sense_description": "subarctic zone of coniferous forest",
                        "target_lang_word": "tajga",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tajga",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee03c869-a4dd-343a-9c66-c2993dfb7aa8",
                                        "entry_id": "46060246-698f-394e-82d6-f89ba8c7a40e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "pásmo jehličnatých lesů v Kanadě a na Sibiři"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eef36ea2-61ab-427e-8f80-890ed0ac0b8f",
                                                "sense_id": "ee03c869-a4dd-343a-9c66-c2993dfb7aa8",
                                                "text": "Tajga byla pokryta sněhem a plná hladových vlků."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4ec7b5f-1d86-4099-aaf3-342751fd9ff3",
                        "source_entry_id": "0ca4b1fc-7f78-3037-8ae3-7981507d040d",
                        "source_sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
                        "source_sense_description": "subarctic zone of coniferous forest",
                        "target_lang_word": "taiga",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "taiga",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39a24c0d-867b-30f8-a51f-44355375bca2",
                                        "entry_id": "984fc7a4-b79c-3545-be2e-c0923378dae5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "een bioom dat wordt gekenmerkt door uitgestrekte, koude en vochtige naaldwouden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b862de3d-8651-4147-a3a9-9d54045a56cc",
                                                "sense_id": "39a24c0d-867b-30f8-a51f-44355375bca2",
                                                "text": "Als je twee paarden op je erf had en twee koeien, was je al koelak. Koelakken werden naar Siberië afgevoerd en daar in een kaal taigabos achtergelaten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4d6bf99-e8d0-4b67-a934-c65b6775d361",
                                                "sense_id": "39a24c0d-867b-30f8-a51f-44355375bca2",
                                                "text": "Het jongetje genaamd Tserin liep zondag achter een puppy aan, het bos in, bekend als de taiga. Die koude en vochtige naaldbossen liggen op de grens tussen toendra en steppen en zitten vol met beren, wolven, lynxen en vossen. Het kind had een reep chocolade bij zich, aldus de grootmoeder."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6195d87f-8e94-4ec2-8d77-fd548f20de38",
                        "source_entry_id": "0ca4b1fc-7f78-3037-8ae3-7981507d040d",
                        "source_sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
                        "source_sense_description": "subarctic zone of coniferous forest",
                        "target_lang_word": "taïga",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "taïga",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01b97ea8-7cbb-3722-8c4c-52a0aaef4455",
                                        "entry_id": "f89deb6c-c13d-3223-b44e-714b1777b6f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Forêt de conifères de climat boréal, dans le nord de l’Europe, de l’Asie et de l’Amérique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e100bfed-5fdb-4595-9e05-1b5ce5e06a5d",
                                                "sense_id": "01b97ea8-7cbb-3722-8c4c-52a0aaef4455",
                                                "text": "Mais il ne s’agit jamais de pergélisol continu. De fait, seule la taïga russe est affectée par ce phénomène."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84fa781b-5ef8-4877-bef4-d854e644a32d",
                                                "sense_id": "01b97ea8-7cbb-3722-8c4c-52a0aaef4455",
                                                "text": "Regarder vers l’est était le pire. La Sibérie orientale et la taïga."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6b25d74-0ba3-4161-9eb6-688f32f59ed4",
                                                "sense_id": "01b97ea8-7cbb-3722-8c4c-52a0aaef4455",
                                                "text": "Bien caché sous mon affût, je contemple le paysage de taïga saupoudré de neige, qui se ternit sous l’étreinte de la nuit et se momifie progressivement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a222693-f3f3-4d29-ac96-138725e6224e",
                        "source_entry_id": "0ca4b1fc-7f78-3037-8ae3-7981507d040d",
                        "source_sense_id": "46d3c489-89f7-30c4-8c48-6747d74a0e00",
